# Code owners for acme-links (the worked example / public exhibit).
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO — stated plainly, because a CODEOWNERS file people believe is
# enforcing when it is not is worse than no file at all.
#
# GitHub only *requires* code-owner review when the branch protection rule for `main` sets
# `require_code_owner_review: true`. It is currently FALSE here (solo-operator model), so this
# file requests review and records privileged surface; it becomes ENFORCING with no further edit
# the day a second maintainer exists.

* @lukasrepublic

# CI — the contract journeys ARE this exhibit's central claim (the money shot is a real red-then-
# green run in this repo's history). A change here changes what the exhibit proves.
/.github/                       @lukasrepublic

# The build-provenance pin: the file that ties this exhibit to the workspace commit its atoms were
# authorized against, and whose own header carries a verification recipe a reader may run.
/.foundry/build-provenance.yaml @lukasrepublic

# Auth and the redirect resolver — the three security-review Blocks found during the build all
# landed in these paths (login CSRF, header-keyed rate limiting, parsed-vs-stored URL).
/src/**/auth/                   @lukasrepublic
/src/**/r/                      @lukasrepublic
